264
00:10:42.669 --> 00:10:44.937
Oh. yeah. I told him
that's what I did.

265
00:10:44.939 --> 00:10:47.973
Hey. what do you think
about a hat?

266
00:10:47.975 --> 00:10:49.641
The only reason
to wear a hat on date

267
00:10:49.643 --> 00:10:50.842
is if you're hiding a bald spot.

268
00:10:50.844 --> 00:10:52.277
Oh.

269
00:10:54.063 --> 00:10:55.697
For your next date.

270
00:10:58.517 --> 00:11:00.369
Thank you.

271
00:11:00.371 --> 00:11:02.520
So you really quit high school?

272
00:11:02.522 --> 00:11:03.655
Mmm. no.

273
00:11:03.657 --> 00:11:05.207
I skipped high school.

274
00:11:05.209 --> 00:11:06.458
I quit MIT.

275
00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.460
Oh. okay. See. there's
the misunderstanding.

276
00:11:08.462 --> 00:11:11.747
Jake has a hard time
spelling MIT.

277
00:11:11.749 --> 00:11:14.466
Oh. Well. then. he really
shouldn't quit school.

278
00:11:14.468 --> 00:11:16.718
Hey. check it out.

279
00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.303
My socks match my sneakers.

280
00:11:18.305 --> 00:11:20.872
But your sneakers
don't match each other.

281
00:11:20.874 --> 00:11:23.892
Oh...

282
00:11:25.061 --> 00:11:27.095
Bridget used to pick out
all my outfits.

283
00:11:27.097 --> 00:11:28.680
I can see why you miss her.

284
00:11:28.682 --> 00:11:31.383
Well. uh. thank you for
clearing the Jake stuff up.

285
00:11:31.385 --> 00:11:32.434
Yeah. no problem.

286
00:11:32.436 --> 00:11:34.102
Uh. and. uh. going forward.

287
00:11:34.104 --> 00:11:36.554
keep in mind that kids like him
are looking for role models.

288
00:11:36.556 --> 00:11:38.223
so you have to be careful
around them.

289
00:11:38.225 --> 00:11:40.142
Yeah. sure.
Although. truth to tell.

290
00:11:40.144 --> 00:11:42.778
unless he sees you passed out
in a pool of vomit

291
00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.997
with a tattooed prostitute.
you're going to be

292
00:11:44.999 --> 00:11:47.082
an improvement
in the role model department.

293
00:11:47.084 --> 00:11:49.952
Hey. Alan?
Yeah?

294
00:11:49.954 --> 00:11:52.570
You got a lot of experience
with women. right?

295
00:11:57.961 --> 00:12:00.578
A lot? (chuckles)
I don't know.

296
00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:04.299
You know. I've. uh. been
around the block a few times.

297
00:12:04.301 --> 00:12:07.436
Did a little dance.
made a little love.

298
00:12:07.438 --> 00:12:10.105
got down tonight
on several occasions.

299
00:12:11.674 --> 00:12:13.025
Um. why do you ask?

300
00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.312
What can I do to convince
Bridget to take me back?

301
00:12:18.147 --> 00:12:19.431
Oh.

302
00:12:19.433 --> 00:12:21.149
(sighs)

303
00:12:21.151 --> 00:12:24.403
Walden. Walden.
Walden. Walden.

304
00:12:24.405 --> 00:12:25.937
Come sit.

305
00:12:25.939 --> 00:12:28.290
Really? I got to sit?

306
00:12:38.134 --> 00:12:42.137
A woman's heart is a deep
and mysterious place.

307
00:12:42.139 --> 00:12:44.289
almost impossible
to reach.

308
00:12:44.291 --> 00:12:46.341
Much like the G-spot.

309
00:12:47.727 --> 00:12:51.463
Although at least we know
the heart. in fact. exists.

310
00:12:51.465 --> 00:12:53.015
Okay. is that it?
Can I stand up now?

311
00:12:53.017 --> 00:12:54.399
Oh. no. H-hang on.
Hang on.

312
00:12:54.401 --> 00:12:57.302
When that heart closes
itself to a man--

313
00:12:57.304 --> 00:12:59.938
and in my experience.
it inevitably does--

314
00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:04.076
the only way to reopen it
is to allow time to pass.

315
00:13:04.078 --> 00:13:06.478
That way. the
woman can reflect

316
00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.664
on how much she
misses her man.

317
00:13:09.499 --> 00:13:10.699
And that's worked
for you?

318
00:13:10.701 --> 00:13:12.984
Oh. yeah.

319
00:13:12.986 --> 00:13:15.704
There are quite a
few ladies out there

320
00:13:15.706 --> 00:13:19.091
currently reflecting on how
much they miss Alan Harper.

321
00:13:19.093 --> 00:13:21.043
Good luck.

322
00:13:23.496 --> 00:13:26.515
Should've asked the kid.

323
00:13:26.517 --> 00:13:28.350
# Men. #

324
00:13:28.352 --> 00:13:29.768
Unbelievable.

325
00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:30.952
You don't like it.

326
00:13:30.954 --> 00:13:32.721
No. no. I blame myself.

327
00:13:32.723 --> 00:13:35.257
I trusted you to make
a simple dinner reservation.

328
00:13:35.259 --> 00:13:37.559
Uh. don't blame me;
blame Jake.

329
00:13:37.561 --> 00:13:38.894
Who's Jake?

330
00:13:38.896 --> 00:13:41.563
He's some kid without a deal.

331
00:13:42.665 --> 00:13:44.449
Besides. does it matter
where we eat

332
00:13:44.451 --> 00:13:46.284
as long as we're
with each other?

333
00:13:46.286 --> 00:13:48.453
(loud clinking)

334
00:13:49.372 --> 00:13:50.789
I got to pee!

335
00:13:50.791 --> 00:13:53.875
Okay. bon appétit.

336
00:13:53.877 --> 00:13:57.129
I got to pee!

337
00:13:57.131 --> 00:13:59.631
Don't you move.

338
00:14:03.436 --> 00:14:04.669
Hello!

339
00:14:04.671 --> 00:14:06.138
(laughs)

340
00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:08.706
She's cute.

341
00:14:08.708 --> 00:14:10.542
You know. it's not too late.

342
00:14:10.544 --> 00:14:11.893
We could still have a kid.

343
00:14:11.895 --> 00:14:13.061
We already do.

344
00:14:13.063 --> 00:14:14.396
I'm looking at him.

345
00:14:14.398 --> 00:14:16.714
Oh. come on.
That's not fair.

346
00:14:16.716 --> 00:14:17.983
Ah. hot soup!

347
00:14:17.985 --> 00:14:20.552
Hot soup. (groans)

348
00:14:21.988 --> 00:14:24.022
Thank you.
Look. Walden.

349
00:14:24.024 --> 00:14:25.407
I agreed to have dinner with you

350
00:14:25.409 --> 00:14:27.325
because I care about you.
but I just...

351
00:14:27.327 --> 00:14:29.077
Are we going to have sex later?

352
00:14:29.079 --> 00:14:30.495
(sighs)
Let me finish.

353
00:14:30.497 --> 00:14:31.830
But no.

354
00:14:31.832 --> 00:14:33.731
Aw.

355
00:14:33.733 --> 00:14:36.034
The thing is.
even though I care about you.

356
00:14:36.036 --> 00:14:37.869
this marriage is over.

357
00:14:37.871 --> 00:14:39.454
I don't want to get
a divorce.

358
00:14:39.456 --> 00:14:41.506
Why do we got to get a divorce?

359
00:14:41.508 --> 00:14:42.624
Because I have grown up

360
00:14:42.626 --> 00:14:44.926
and you are still the same guy
you were at 19.

361
00:14:44.928 --> 00:14:45.961
No. that is not true.

362
00:14:45.963 --> 00:14:47.095
I got a lot more money now.

363
00:14:47.097 --> 00:14:48.346
Money isn't the point.

364
00:14:48.348 --> 00:14:49.931
I got lawyers.
I got accountants.

365
00:14:49.933 --> 00:14:51.749
I got my own
charitable foundation.

366
00:14:51.751 --> 00:14:54.186
It's not about what you have;
it's about who you are.

367
00:14:54.188 --> 00:14:55.353
Oh.

368
00:14:55.355 --> 00:14:57.606
Well. I'm pretty much
the same guy.

369
00:14:57.608 --> 00:15:00.392
What I want. what I need.
is a partner in life.

370
00:15:00.394 --> 00:15:03.945
A grown-up. mature.
responsible adult.

371
00:15:03.947 --> 00:15:05.313
What. and you don't think
that's me?

372
00:15:05.315 --> 00:15:06.764
No. I don't.

373
00:15:09.285 --> 00:15:10.768
And you don't think
I can change?

374
00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:12.070
No. I don't.
But what if I can?

375
00:15:12.072 --> 00:15:13.121
But you can't.
Can. too.

376
00:15:13.123 --> 00:15:14.656
Just eat your dinner.

377
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.577
Ugh.

378
00:15:18.579 --> 00:15:19.795
This blows.

379
00:15:19.797 --> 00:15:21.379
I know. but it's something

380
00:15:21.381 --> 00:15:23.632
we're both just going
to have to accept.

381
00:15:25.218 --> 00:15:27.285
How's your beach house?

382
00:15:27.287 --> 00:15:29.471
It's okay.

383
00:15:30.506 --> 00:15:31.840
But I miss you.

384
00:15:31.842 --> 00:15:33.842
I miss you. too. sometimes.

385
00:15:33.844 --> 00:15:34.810
Really?

386
00:15:34.812 --> 00:15:36.895
Walden. we were together
for 15 years.

387
00:15:36.897 --> 00:15:39.147
Those feelings
don't just go away.

388
00:15:40.817 --> 00:15:42.484
(laughing)

389
00:15:42.486 --> 00:15:45.654
Hey. be cool.

390
00:15:46.772 --> 00:15:49.974
So. uh. you really still have
feelings for me?

391
00:15:49.976 --> 00:15:52.360
Of course I do.
Oh.

392
00:15:52.362 --> 00:15:53.645
(laughing)

393
00:15:53.647 --> 00:15:55.113
Hey.

394
00:15:55.115 --> 00:15:57.666
Big girls don't throw food.

395
00:15:59.252 --> 00:16:01.586
Trust me. I can change.

396
00:16:01.588 --> 00:16:03.154
I really can.

397
00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:05.257
(laughs)

398
00:16:05.259 --> 00:16:06.341
All right. that's it.
Eat lettuce!

399
00:16:06.343 --> 00:16:09.044
Walden!
What? She started it.

400
00:16:09.046 --> 00:16:10.178
Whoa! No pasta.

401
00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:11.630
I call no pasta.

402
00:16:11.632 --> 00:16:14.249
(laughing)

403
00:16:14.251 --> 00:16:15.667
Oh. it is on!

404
00:16:16.519 --> 00:16:17.769
Oh. yeah.

405
00:16:17.771 --> 00:16:19.554
And she got some...
Here it comes.

406
00:16:19.556 --> 00:16:20.889
Here it comes.
Here it comes.

407
00:16:20.891 --> 00:16:21.973
(whooping)

408
00:16:21.975 --> 00:16:23.942
# Men. #

409
00:16:23.944 --> 00:16:25.644
(doorbell rings)

410
00:16:25.646 --> 00:16:27.362
Berta. can you
get the door?

411
00:16:27.364 --> 00:16:29.814
I'm off the clock. Zippy.

412
00:16:29.816 --> 00:16:31.650
What clock?
You're a live-in.

413
00:16:31.652 --> 00:16:33.952
And I'm livin'.

414
00:16:39.292 --> 00:16:42.511
You know you took
the wrong brother. right?

415
00:16:44.196 --> 00:16:45.580
Judith. what are
you doing here?

416
00:16:45.582 --> 00:16:47.169
Why did you tell Jake
he could quit school?

417
00:16:47.217 --> 00:16:48.169
I didn't.

418
00:16:48.194 --> 00:16:49.465
Well. then. where
did he get the idea?

419
00:16:49.469 --> 00:16:51.419
Walden. He told him
about how when he quit

420
00:16:51.421 --> 00:16:52.870
he made hundreds of
millions of dollars.

421
00:16:52.872 --> 00:16:54.806
and now Jake thinks
he can do it. too.

422
00:16:54.808 --> 00:16:56.391
Terrific.
And I thought your brother

423
00:16:56.393 --> 00:16:57.893
was a horrible influence.

424
00:16:57.895 --> 00:16:59.594
Don't speak ill
of the dead.

425
00:16:59.596 --> 00:17:02.180
But you're right-- he was
a terrible human being.

426
00:17:02.182 --> 00:17:04.933
Hey. who's at
the... Whoops!

427
00:17:04.935 --> 00:17:07.652
You come back
here. young man!

428
00:17:08.654 --> 00:17:10.238
He's not coming back. is he?

429
00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.073
I wouldn't.

430
00:17:13.058 --> 00:17:14.492
Hey.

431
00:17:14.494 --> 00:17:16.778
Walden. I want a word with you.

432
00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:18.747
Walden. you remember
Judith. Bye.

433
00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:22.584
You're Alan's ex. right?

434
00:17:22.586 --> 00:17:24.452
Yes. and Jake's mother.

435
00:17:24.454 --> 00:17:26.037
And you and I need
to discuss how...

436
00:17:26.039 --> 00:17:27.422
I just had dinner
with my ex.

437
00:17:27.424 --> 00:17:28.740
Well. that's very
nice. Anyway...

438
00:17:28.742 --> 00:17:30.342
She's not my ex yet.
but she's going to be.

439
00:17:30.344 --> 00:17:31.593
I'm sorry.

440
00:17:31.595 --> 00:17:34.429
She hates me.
but I'm still in love with her.

441
00:17:34.431 --> 00:17:37.299
Well. I'm sure you'll find
somebody else.

442
00:17:38.718 --> 00:17:42.253
Since we were teenagers.
she's been the only one.

443
00:17:42.255 --> 00:17:44.105
You were high school
sweethearts?

444
00:17:44.107 --> 00:17:46.308
Yeah.

445
00:17:49.145 --> 00:17:51.363
That is so romantic.

446
00:17:55.985 --> 00:17:59.120
And I blew it again tonight.

447
00:17:59.122 --> 00:18:00.605
Oh. Hey. come on now.

448
00:18:00.607 --> 00:18:02.073
It... it'll be okay.

449
00:18:02.075 --> 00:18:04.793
No. it'll never be okay.

450
00:18:06.128 --> 00:18:08.129
She's my soul mate.

451
00:18:08.131 --> 00:18:11.583
Oh. you poor.
sweet man.

452
00:18:12.918 --> 00:18:16.421
Who smells like ranch dressing
and fettuccine alfredo.

453
00:18:17.306 --> 00:18:19.341
Have you ever loved
anyone like that?

454
00:18:20.676 --> 00:18:22.477
No.

455
00:18:22.479 --> 00:18:25.013
Don't. 'cause it
hurts too much.

456
00:18:25.015 --> 00:18:27.315
Oh. I wish there was
something I could do.

457
00:18:27.317 --> 00:18:29.234
Like what?

458
00:18:41.547 --> 00:18:43.698
Oh. yeah.
I'm so quitting high school.

459
00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.950
# Men. #

460
00:18:49.362 --> 00:18:50.428
# Men. #

461
00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:51.996
For the last time. Jake.

462
00:18:51.998 --> 00:18:53.948
you're not dropping out
of high school.

463
00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.384
What if I can convince Mom
to let me?

464
00:18:56.386 --> 00:18:57.919
(laughs) Sure.

465
00:18:57.921 --> 00:19:01.389
If your mother says it's okay.
you can have my blessing.

466
00:19:02.224 --> 00:19:04.458
Cool.

467
00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.428
And while I'm at it.
I'll buy you a car.

468
00:19:08.308 --> 00:19:10.693
Oh. no. no. a space ship.

469
00:19:11.234 --> 00:19:13.014
Car's fine.

470
00:19:13.015 --> 00:19:14.181
Good night. Jake.

471
00:19:14.183 --> 00:19:15.449
Good night. Dad.

472
00:19:16.684 --> 00:19:18.485
(passing gas)

473
00:19:18.487 --> 00:19:20.654
That...
that was the air mattress.

474
00:19:20.656 --> 00:19:22.389
Okay.

475
00:19:23.691 --> 00:19:25.993
(passing gas)

476
00:19:27.061 --> 00:19:28.962
That was me.

477
00:19:29.797 --> 00:19:32.649
(panting)

478
00:19:32.651 --> 00:19:34.651
Holy moly.

479
00:19:34.653 --> 00:19:36.787
What got into
you tonight?

480
00:19:36.789 --> 00:19:39.756
<i>You know.
besides moi.</i>

481
00:19:41.009 --> 00:19:42.459
Shh. Don't talk.

482
00:19:42.461 --> 00:19:44.094
Okay.

483
00:19:44.096 --> 00:19:46.346
(sighs)

484
00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:49.486
How would you feel
about growing a beard?

485
00:19:50.932 --> 00:19:52.382
Wouldn't that
scratch your face?

486
00:19:54.203 --> 00:19:55.535
Yeah.
